Jbofi'e's often nonexistent error messages are extremely frustrating,
to be sure. Lojgloss should never have that. (It does happen
sometimes, but those are always bugs that are usually pretty simple to
fix.)

So I'm wondering how many of you would be satisfied with (A) simply
knowing how far into the parsed text the parser got (the more advanced
students of Lojban, I assume), i.e. *where* the error happened, and
how many of you would like to (B) have more detail, in the form of a
somewhat cryptic tree of parsing information that can potentially
assist you, but might require a bit of puzzling over. Please vote at
http://www.micropoll.com/akira/mpview/622722-182488

BTW, I'm looking into permanent external hosting for Lojgloss, which
is currently run from my home machine, and currently down (because of
my mabla ISP).

